<% content_for :title, "Dashboard - #{@partner.name}" %>

<div class="px-4 py-6 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <%#
    The status pill that used to sit in `actions:` is a callout instead, and only when it has
    something to say.

    It could not stay: a status is not an action, and `actions:` is documented as "at most three,
    exactly one primary". It could not move to `status:` either, the way the profile's did -- that
    slot renders on the title line, and this title is a page rather than the agency, so the heading
    would have read "Dashboard Approved". Retitling the page to the agency's name was tried and
    reverted: a spec asserts `h1` text "Dashboard" to prove a redirect landed here, which is a fair
    use of a heading that names its page.

    A callout is the better answer anyway, because the pill was doing a job it was bad at. The
    request options card below is hidden outright for a partner who is not approved, and the pill
    was the only thing on the page explaining why -- a word in the corner, next to a page title,
    with no statement of consequence. And for the approved majority it said "Approved" every day,
    which is noise. `partners/profiles/show` already answers a status this way, with a callout for
    `recertification_required`; this is the same pattern.
  %>
  <%# A sentence per state rather than the humanized enum: "Your agency is recertification
      required" is a column value, not something anyone says. Each one names the consequence --
      you cannot make requests -- because that is the change the reader is trying to explain. %>
  <% unless @partner.approved? %>
    <%= render "shared/essentials/callout",
          tone: (@partner.deactivated? ? :danger : :warning), wrapper_class: "mb-6" do %>
      <% if @partner.deactivated? %>
        Your agency is deactivated, so you cannot make requests. Contact your bank if that is unexpected.
      <% elsif @partner.recertification_required? %>
        Your agency needs recertifying before you can make requests again. Review your profile and
        submit it for approval.
      <% else %>
        Your agency is waiting for your bank to approve it. You will be able to make requests once
        it has.
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "shared/essentials/page_header",
        title: "Dashboard",
        subtitle: "News from your bank, and what is coming or already delivered." %>

  <div class="space-y-6">
    <%= render "broadcast_announcement" if @broadcast_announcements.any? %>

    <% if @partner.info_for_partner.present? %>
      <%= render "shared/essentials/card", title: "Information from #{@parent_org.name}" do %>
        <div class="text-sm text-slate-700"><%= @partner.info_for_partner %></div>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>

    <%= render partial: "/partners/requests/request_options_card" if @partner.approved? %>
    <%= render partial: "requests_in_progress" %>

    <%= render partial: "partners/distributions/distribution_section",
          locals: {distributions: @upcoming_distributions,
                   title: "Upcoming distributions", date_header: "Pick up date",
                   item_header: "Items to receive"} %>

    <%= render partial: "partners/distributions/distribution_section",
          locals: {distributions: @distributions,
                   title: "Prior distributions", date_header: "Date received",
                   item_header: "Items received"} %>

    <%= render partial: "family_details" %>
  </div>
</div>
